WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.870
Your first AI skill felt like magic.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:04.850
By skill number 20,

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.990
you almost need a skill to manage your skills.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.770
That's because more skills bring predictable problems.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.010
Your skill and a company skill sound alike,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.730
and the wrong one runs.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.770
And several skills repeat the same research.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.090
Other skills run slowly, give different results each time, or get forgotten.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.410
It's like a ring of look-alike keys:

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.580
the right one is always the last you try.

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:34.840
But each problem has a matching pattern.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:39.200
Repeated parts become small skills that one main skill runs in order.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.520
And a skill that needs more knowledge carries it in its own files,

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.640
so it works for a teammate too.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:50.640
So in this adventure, you audit your skills and fix what costs you most,

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:54.280
or build a more sophisticated skill with the same patterns.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:56.860
Then you test it on real work.
